+    {"Jewellery can be <w>%</w>ut on or <w>%</w>emoved again", "首饰可以<w>%</w>戴上或<w>%</w>取下"},
+    {", though in Tiles, either can be done by clicking on the item in your inventory", "，不过在 Tiles 模式下，两者都可通过点击物品栏中的物品完成"},
+    {"\n\nThis ", "\n\n这 "},
+    {" offers its wearer protection from certain sources. For an overview of your resistances (among other things) press <w>%</w>", " 为其佩戴者提供对某些来源的保护。要查看你的抗性总览（以及其他信息），请按 <w>%</w>"},
+    {"\n\nWhen worn, some types of jewellery (such as this one) offer certain <w>%</w>bilities you can activate. ", "\n\n佩戴时，某些类型的首饰（例如这件）会提供你可以激活的<w>%</w>能力。 "},
+    {"Press <w>%</w> to quaff this potion", "按 <w>%</w> 饮下此药水"},
+    {"A manual can greatly help you in training a skill. After you pick one up, the skill in question will be trained more efficiently and will level up faster until you exhaust the manual's contents.", "手册能极大帮助你训练某项技能。拾取后，相关技能会训练得更高效、升级更快，直到你耗尽手册的内容。"},
+    {"\nYou can pick up a spellbook to add its spells to your spell library. (View your spell library with <w>%</w>.)", "\n你可以拾取法术书，将其法术加入你的法术库。（用 <w>%</w> 查看法术库。）"},
+    {"Skeletons and corpses can be used as components for certain necromantic spells. Apart from that, they are largely useless.", "骷髅和尸体可作为某些死灵法术的材料。除此之外，它们基本没什么用。"},
+    {"This staff can enhance your spellcasting, making spells of its related spell school more powerful.", "这根法杖能增强你的施法，使其相关法术学派的法术更强大。"},
+    {"It also offers its wielder protection from certain sources. For an overview of your resistances (among other things) press <w>%</w>", "它还会为其持有者提供对某些来源的保护。要查看你的抗性总览（以及其他信息），请按 <w>%</w>"},
+    {"\n\nSeeing how ", "\n\n鉴于 "},
+    {" frowns upon the use of magic, this staff will be of little use to you and you might just as well <w>%</w>rop it now.", " 不赞成使用魔法，这根法杖对你用处不大，你不如现在就<w>%</w>丢弃它。"},
+    {"Miscellaneous items sometimes harbour magical powers that can be harnessed by e<w>%</w>oking the item.", "杂项物品有时蕴含魔法力量，可通过<w>%</w>激发该物品来加以利用。"},
+    {"These nasty constructions can cause a range of unpleasant effects. You won't be able to avoid tripping traps by flying over them; their magic construction will cause them to be triggered anyway.", "这些讨厌的装置会引发各种令人不适的效果。你无法靠飞越来避免触发陷阱；其魔法构造无论如何都会使其被触发。"},
+    {"The dungeon contains a number of natural obstacles such as shafts, which lead one to three levels down. Once you know the shaft is there, you can safely step over it.\nIf you want to jump down there, use <w>></w> to do so. Be warned that getting back here might be difficult.", "地牢中有一些天然障碍，例如竖井，可通往下方一至三层。一旦你知道竖井在那里，就能安全地跨过它。\n如果你想跳下去，按 <w>></w> 即可。请注意，回到这里可能会很困难。"},
+    {"Some areas of the dungeon, such as the Spider Nest, may be strewn with giant webs that may ensnare you for a short time. Insects, oozes and incorporeal entities can navigate the webs safely.", "地牢的某些区域，如蜘蛛巢穴，可能布满巨型蛛网，会短暂缠住你。昆虫、软泥和非实体存在可以安全地在蛛网中穿行。"},
+    {"You can enter the next (deeper) level by following them down (<w>></w>). To get back to this level again, press <w><<</w> while standing on the upstairs.", "你可以沿着它们向下（<w>></w>）进入下一层（更深）。要返回本层，站在上行楼梯上按 <w><<</w>。"},
+    {" In Tiles, you can achieve the same, in either direction, by clicking the <w>left mouse button</w>.", " 在 Tiles 模式下，你可以用<w>鼠标左键</w>点击来实现任一方向的相同操作。"},
+    {"\n\nYou have not yet passed through this particular set of stairs. ", "\n\n你尚未通过这组特定的楼梯。 "},
+    {"These stairs lead out of the dungeon. Following them will end the game. The only way to win is to transport the fabled Orb of Zot outside.", "这些楼梯通往地牢之外。沿着它们走会结束游戏。获胜的唯一方法是将传说中的佐特宝珠运送出去。"},
+    {"You can enter the previous (shallower) level by following these up (<w><<</w>). This is ideal for retreating or finding a safe resting spot, since the previous level will have less monsters, and monsters on this level can't follow you up unless they're standing right next to you. To get back to this level again, press <w>></w> while standing on the downstairs.", "你可以沿着这些楼梯向上（<w><<</w>）进入上一层（更浅）。这非常适合撤退或寻找安全的休息点，因为上一层的怪物更少，而本层的怪物除非紧挨着你，否则无法跟随你上楼。要返回本层，站在下行楼梯上按 <w>></w>。"},
+    {" In Tiles, you can perform either action simply by clicking the <w>left mouse button</w> instead.", " 在 Tiles 模式下，你只需点击<w>鼠标左键</w>即可执行任一操作。"},
+    {"Escape hatches can be used to quickly leave a level with <w><<</w> and <w>></w>, respectively. Note that you will usually be unable to return right away.", "逃生出口可用于快速离开当前层，分别使用 <w><<</w> 和 <w>></w>。注意，你通常无法立即返回。"},
+    {"\nTo avoid accidentally opening a door you'd rather remain closed during travel or autoexplore, you can mark it with an exclusion from the map view (<w>X</w>) with <w>ee</w> while your cursor is on the grid in question. Such an exclusion will prevent autotravel from ever entering that grid until you remove the exclusion with another press of <w>Xe</w>.", "\n为避免在旅行或自动探索时意外打开你想保持关闭的门，你可以在光标位于相应格子时，从地图视图（<w>X</w>）用 <w>ee</w> 将其标记为排除。此排除会阻止自动旅行进入该格子，直到你再次按 <w>Xe</w> 移除排除。"},
+    {"This is your chance to join a religion! In general, the gods will help their followers, bestowing powers of all sorts upon them, but many of them demand a life of dedication, constant tributes or entertainment in return.\n", "这是你加入宗教的机会！一般来说，众神会帮助其信徒，赐予他们各种力量，但许多神要求以奉献的一生、不断的供奉或娱乐作为回报。\n"},
+    {"This particular altar is so ancient that you cannot make out which god it is dedicated to! Converting here by pressing <w>></w> while standing on the altar will enter you into service of a random god, who will grant you some additional piety in thanks.", "这座祭坛太过古老，你无法辨认它供奉的是哪位神！站在祭坛上按 <w>></w> 皈依，会让你进入某位随机神的服务，作为感谢，他会赐予你一些额外的虔诚。"},
+    {"You can get information about <w>", "你可以获取关于 <w>"},
+    {"</w> by pressing <w>></w> while standing on the altar. Before taking up the responding faith you'll be asked for confirmation.", "</w> 的信息，方法是站在祭坛上按 <w>></w>。在皈依相应信仰之前，系统会要求你确认。"},
+    {"This particular altar is so ancient that you cannot make out which god it is dedicated to, and ", "这座祭坛太过古老，你无法辨认它供奉的是哪位神，而且 "},
+    {" probably won't like it if you switch allegiance. If you want to take the risk, you can convert here by pressing <w>></w> while standing on the altar. Doing so will enter you into service of a random god, who will grant you some additional piety in thanks.", " 很可能不喜欢你改变效忠对象。如果你想冒险，可以站在祭坛上按 <w>></w> 在此皈依。这样做会让你进入某位随机神的服务，作为感谢，他会赐予你一些额外的虔诚。"},
+    {" probably won't like it if you switch allegiance, but having a look won't hurt: to get information on <w>", " 很可能不喜欢你改变效忠对象，但看一眼无妨：要获取关于 <w>"},
+    {"</w>, press <w>></w> while standing on the altar. Before taking up the responding faith (and abandoning your current one!) you'll be asked for confirmation.\nTo see your current standing with ", "</w> 的信息，站在祭坛上按 <w>></w>。在皈依相应信仰（并抛弃你当前的信仰！）之前，系统会要求你确认。\n要查看你与 "},
+    {" press <w>^</w>", " 的当前关系，请按 <w>^</w>"},
+    {", or click with your <w>right mouse button</w> on your avatar while pressing <w>Shift</w>", "，或在按住 <w>Shift</w> 的同时用<w>鼠标右键</w>点击你的角色"},
+    {"An entryway into one of the many dungeon side branches in Crawl. ", "通往 Crawl 众多地牢支线之一的入口。 "},
+    {"Beware, sometimes these can be deadly!", "当心，有时这些会很致命！"},
+    {"are ", "是 "},
+    {"harmless. ", "无害的。 "},
+    {"probably dangerous, and you should stay out of it if you can. ", "可能很危险，如果可以，你应远离它。 "},
+    {"currently harmless, but that could change at some point. Check the overview screen (<w>%</w>) to view your resistances.", "目前无害，但随时可能改变。查看总览界面（<w>%</w>）以了解你的抗性。"},
+    {"\nThis cloud", "\n这团云雾"},
+    {" is opaque. If two or more opaque clouds are between you and a square, you won't be able to see anything in that square.", " 是不透明的。如果有两团或更多不透明云雾位于你与某格之间，你将无法看到该格中的任何东西。"},
+    {"Did you think you were the only adventurer in the dungeon? Well, you thought wrong! These unique adversaries often possess skills that normal monsters wouldn't, so be careful.\n\n", "你以为你是地牢中唯一的冒险者？那你可想错了！这些独特的对手往往拥有普通怪物所没有的技能，所以要小心。\n\n"},
+    {"The ghost of a deceased adventurer, it would like nothing better than to send you the same way.\n\n", "一位已故冒险者的幽灵，它最想做的就是让你也步其后尘。\n\n"},
+    {"This monster appears to be really dangerous!\n", "这只怪物看起来非常危险！\n"},
+    {"This monster appears to be quite dangerous.\n", "这只怪物看起来相当危险。\n"},
+    {"A berserking monster is bloodthirsty and fighting madly. Such a blood rage makes it particularly dangerous!\n\n", "狂暴的怪物嗜血且疯狂战斗。这种血怒使它格外危险！\n\n"},
+    {"Friendly monsters will follow you around and attempt to aid you in battle. You can order nearby allies by <w>t</w>alking to them.", "友好怪物会跟随你并在战斗中协助你。你可以通过<w>t</w>与它们交谈来指挥附近的盟友。"},
+    {"\n\nHowever, it is only <w>temporarily</w> friendly, and will become dangerous again when this friendliness wears off.", "\n\n不过，它只是<w>暂时</w>友好，当这种友好消退后会再次变得危险。"},
+    {"You can easily mark its square as dangerous to avoid accidentally entering into its field of view when using auto-explore or auto-travel. To do so, enter targeting mode with <w>x</w> and then press <w>e</w> when your cursor is hovering over the monster's grid. Doing so will mark this grid and all surrounding ones within a radius of 8 as \"excluded\" ones that explore or travel modes won't enter.", "你可以轻松将其所在格子标记为危险，以免在使用自动探索或自动旅行时意外进入其视野。要做到这一点，按 <w>x</w> 进入目标模式，然后将光标悬停在怪物所在格子上并按 <w>e</w>。这样做会将此格子及周围半径 8 以内的所有格子标记为“排除”，探索或旅行模式不会进入。"},
+    {"This might be a good time to run away", "现在或许是逃跑的好时机"},
+    {" or apply your Berserk <w>a</w>bility", " 或使用你的狂暴<w>a</w>能力"},
+    {"Apparently it has not noticed you - yet. Note that you do not have to engage every monster you meet. Sometimes, discretion is the better part of valour.", "看来它还没有注意到你——暂时如此。注意，你不必与遇到的每只怪物交战。有时，谨慎比勇敢更重要。"},
+    {"Apparently it has been distracted by something. You could use this opportunity to sneak up on this monster - or to sneak away.", "看来它被什么东西分散了注意力。你可以趁机悄悄接近这只怪物——或者悄悄溜走。"},
+    {"\nThis monster doesn't appear to have any resistances or susceptibilities. It cannot fly and is of average speed. Examining other, possibly more high-level monsters can give important clues as to how to deal with them.", "\n这只怪物似乎没有任何抗性或弱点。它不会飞，速度普通。检视其他可能更高等级的怪物，可以获得如何应对它们的重要线索。"},
