+    {"“Mother, I kneel before gold,\n my lover and beloved;\n and knowing I adore him,\n he turns melancholic yellow.\n Because he follows his every lust\n whether doubloon or dust,\n a mighty knight\n is Don Dinero.”\n    -Francisco de Quevedo, _Poderoso caballero es don Dinero_. 1603.\n     trans. Christopher Johnson, 2009.", "“母亲啊，我跪伏在黄金面前，\n 我的爱人与心上人；\n 他既知我倾慕于他，\n 便化作忧郁的黄色。\n 只因他追随自己每一桩欲望，\n 无论是金币还是尘土，\n 一位强大的骑士\n 正是金钱老爷。”\n    -弗朗西斯科·德·克维多，《强大的骑士是金钱老爷》。1603年。\n     克里斯托弗·约翰逊 译，2009年。"},
+    {"“Now Absalom in his lifetime had taken and reared up for himself a pillar,\n which is in the king's dale: for he said, I have no son to keep my name in\n remembrance...”\n    -KJV Bible, 2 Samuel 18:18.", "“押沙龙在世时，曾为自己立了一根柱子，\n 立在王谷中；因为他说，我没有儿子为我留名\n 作纪念……”\n    -钦定版圣经，撒母耳记下 18:18。"},
+    {"“There is shadow under this red rock,\n (Come in under the shadow of this red rock),\n And I will show you something different from either\n Your shadow at morning striding behind you\n Or your shadow at evening rising to meet you;\n I will show you fear in a handful of dust.”\n    -T.S. Eliot, “The Waste Land”. 1922", "“这红色岩石下有一片阴影，\n （到这块红岩的阴影里来吧），\n 我要让你看见一样东西，与你\n 清晨在你身后行走的影子不同，\n 也与你黄昏时起身迎接你的影子不同；\n 我要在一把尘土中让你看见恐惧。”\n    -T.S. 艾略特，《荒原》。1922年"},
+    {"<Desolation>", "<荒芜>"},
+    {"“Then Paul stood in the midst of Mars' hill, and said, Ye men of Athens, I\n perceive that in all things ye are too superstitious. For as I passed by, and\n beheld your devotions, I found an altar with this inscription, TO THE UNKNOWN\n GOD.”\n    -KJV Bible, Acts 17:22-23.", "“保罗站在亚略巴古当中，说，雅典的诸位，我\n看你们凡事都过于敬畏鬼神。因为我从你们中间经过，\n观看你们所敬拜的，遇见一座坛，上面写着，未识之\n神。”\n    -钦定版圣经，使徒行传 17:22-23。"},
+    {"“We made an expedition;\n We met a host and quelled it;\n We forced a strong position,\n And killed the men who held it.\n ...\n“Fierce warriors rushed to meet us;\n We met them, and o’erthrew them:\n They struggled hard to beat us;\n But we conquered them, and slew them.”\n    -Thomas Love Peacock, “The War Song of Dinas Vawr”. 1829.", "“我们出师远征；\n 遇上一支军队，将其击溃；\n 我们强攻下一处坚垒，\n 杀死了据守其中的人。\n ……\n“凶猛的战士冲上来迎战我们；\n 我们迎上去，把他们掀翻：\n 他们奋力想要打败我们；\n 但我们征服了他们，把他们杀死。”\n    -托马斯·拉夫·皮科克，《迪纳斯沃的战歌》。1829年。"},
+    {"“O Progeny of Heaven! Empyreal Thrones!\n With reason hath deep silence and demur\n Seized us, though undismayed. Long is the way\n And hard, that out of Hell leads up to light.”\n    -John Milton, _Paradise Lost_. 1674 (2nd Ed.).", "“天堂的子孙啊！高天的众宝座啊！\n 深深的沉默与迟疑自有理由地\n 攫住了我们，尽管我们并未气馁。漫长而艰险，\n 是那从地狱通向光明的路。”\n    -约翰·弥尔顿，《失乐园》。1674年（第二版）。"},
